    "result": "PASS (indirect; no row or log records the prior state)",
    "detail": "399 of 400 seeds differ between D and P in steps, final state or resolution counts (398 in steps, 379 in final state, 169 in final floor, 144 in final hp, 399 in resolution counts); 85 differ in A10 outcome, 100 in the A9 estimate. The one identical seed, 91000303, is an 84-step act-1 death on floor 8 (wall 7.04 s vs 7.02 s), the kind of run that can end before any elite or boss room, where the prior never acts. Runs are seed-deterministic on this .so (ship identity record), so if STS2_RUNAI_PRIOR_NET=off had not engaged, or the wheel had no built-in prior, P would equal D on every seed. The wheel does carry the prior: builtin_prior_net_json('Ironclad') returns 268,757 bytes, sha256 ca4692595c22...d4f2, and None for the other four characters (checked now; .so sha256 still 823fa393...). Which arm had the prior rests on run_eval.sh: D gets no extra env, P gets `env STS2_RUNAI_PRIOR_NET=off`. A labelling swap would leave the discordance unchanged, so it is not ruled out by the rows; the per-step cost (D 1.04x P) is in the direction the prior's extra work predicts, but that is weak.",
    "logs": "logs/D.stdout and logs/P.stdout contain no line naming the prior or any STS2_* env; both stderr files are 0 bytes. driver.log's env line for P does not show STS2_RUNAI_PRIOR_NET because `env` applies it to the child after the line is logged. Both stdouts report 'G1b ownership audit: PASS'."
